,317,7633,2877,12950,18,11,15,29621,7,18,4999,18,29621,7,15,4999,18,29621,7,15,11,15,1106,7633,2877,12950,15,11,15,29621,4080,19,11,15,29621,4080,19,11,19,29621,7,15,11,19,1106,7633,2877,11,13418,4080,17,13,19,11,17,13,17,4806,16213,7,24,15,481,264,76097,7,19,14,18,31870,1188,18,11,15,29621,7,23,11,15,29621,7,23,4999,20,29621,7,18,4999,20,4945,718,8762,26483,11,16213,4080,16,18,15,4806,64,317,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nSquares are constructed on each of the sides of triangle $\\triangle ABC$, as shown.  If the perimeter of $\\triangle ABC$ is 17, then what is the perimeter of the nine-sided figure that is composed of the remaining three sides of each of the squares? [asy]\nimport olympiad; size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); dotfactor=4;\npicture a;\ndraw(a,(0,0)--(3,0)--(0,4)--cycle);\nlabel(\"$A$\",(-2.1,-2.2),SW);\nlabel(\"$B$\",(3.1,-2.2),SE);\nlabel(\"$C$\",(0.05,0.3),N);\ndraw(a,(3,0)--(3,-3)--(0,-3)--(0,0));\ndraw(a,(0,0)--(-4,0)--(-4,4)--(0,4));\ndraw(a,shift(-2.4,2.2)*rotate(90 - aTan(4/3))*((3,0)--(8,0)--(8,-5)--(3,-5)));\nadd(currentpicture,rotate(-130)*a);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"ca3c2f97cee8c3cdde9276e00aae6f47eb3382779ee49868b3abc602df4a1a60"},"seconds":9.298625230789185,"seed":615440041902481912,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to determine the perimeter of the nine-sided figure formed by the remaining three sides of each square constructed on the sides of triangle \\( \\triangle ABC \\).\n\nFirst, let's denote the sides of \\( \\triangle ABC \\) as follows:\n- \\( AB = c \\)\n- \\( BC = a \\)\n- \\( CA = b \\)\n\nThe perimeter of \\( \\triangle ABC \\) is given as 17, so we have:\n\\[\na + b + c = 17\n\\]\n\nNext, we construct squares on each side of \\( \\triangle ABC \\):\n- A square on side \\( AB \\) with side length \\( c \\)\n- A square on side \\( BC \\) with side length \\( a \\)\n- A square on side \\( CA \\) with side length \\( b \\)\n\nEach square has four sides, but we are interested in the remaining three sides of each square that form the nine-sided figure.\n\nFor each square:\n- The side length of the square is the same as the side length of the triangle.\n- Each square has three remaining sides that contribute to the perimeter of the nine-sided figure.\n\nThus, the total contribution to the perimeter from each square is:\n\\[\n3c, \\quad 3a, \\quad 3b\n\\]\n\nSumming these contributions, we get:\n\\[\n3c + 3a + 3b\n\\]\n\nWe can factor out the 3:\n\\[\n3(a + b + c)\n\\]\n\nSince \\( a + b + c = 17 \\), we substitute this value in:\n\\[\n3 \\times 17 = 51\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the perimeter of the nine-sided figure is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{51}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{51}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:179"}
